      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Modulo and Overflow: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Definition and Safe Operations",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`a mod m` = remainder in ==[0, m-1]==",
                "`a ≡ b (mod m)` means ==m divides (a-b)==",
                "Reduce at every step: `(a*b) % m = ((a%m)*(b%m)) % m`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Op",
                "Reduce each step?",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`+` `-` `*`",
                  "{green:Safe}",
                  "reduce after each"
                ],
                [
                  "`/`",
                  "{red:Not allowed}",
                  "`(a/b)%m ≠ (a%m)/(b%m)`; use the modular inverse"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Negative Operands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "int r = ((a % m) + m) % m;"
              ],
              "note": "C++/Java: -7 % 5 = -2; the fix gives 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Overflow with 1e9+7",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "a, b < 1e9+7",
                    "sub": "prime modulus",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a*b ≈ 1e18",
                    "sub": "too big for int",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "long long",
                    "sub": "64-bit",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "% m",
                    "sub": "after each multiply",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Multiply in `int`, or reduce only at the end: the product ==overflows==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why no direct division?** Use the modular inverse instead.",
                "**-7 % 5 in C++?** -2; use `((a%m)+m)%m` for 3.",
                "**Why long long?** Products reach about 1e18."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "GCD, Euclid and LCM",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "GCD, Euclid and LCM",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Euclid's Rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==gcd(a,b) = gcd(b, a % b)==",
                "Stop when ==b = 0==, return **a**; so gcd(0,x) = x",
                "Time ==O(log(min(a,b)))==: the remainder at least halves every two steps"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "int gcd(int a,int b){",
                "    return b==0 ? a : gcd(b, a%b);",
                "}",
                "// C++17: std::gcd(a, b) in <numeric>"
              ],
              "note": "recursive form or the built-in"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Trace and LCM",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "gcd(48,18)",
                    "sub": "48 % 18 = 12",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "gcd(18,12)",
                    "sub": "18 % 12 = 6",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "gcd(12,6)",
                    "sub": "12 % 6 = 0",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "gcd(6,0) = 6",
                    "sub": "b = 0, stop",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==lcm(a,b) = a / gcd(a,b) * b==",
                "lcm(48,18) = 48/6*18 = {green:144}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Identities",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fact",
                "Why it matters"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`gcd(a,b) * lcm(a,b) = a*b`",
                  "gives lcm from gcd"
                ],
                [
                  "Extended Euclid: `ax + by = gcd(a,b)`",
                  "finds x and y"
                ],
                [
                  "Extended Euclid",
                  "base of the ==modular inverse=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "LCM overflow",
              "text": "**Divide first**: `a / gcd * b`. Never `a*b/gcd`, because a*b overflows before the division."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Primes and the Sieve of Eratosthenes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Primes and the Sieve of Eratosthenes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Trial Division",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:n < 2} is ==not prime==",
                "Test divisors `i` while ==i*i <= n==",
                "Cost: **O(sqrt n)** per number"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Sieve",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "For each prime `p` up to ==sqrt(n)==, mark its multiples composite",
                "Start marking at ==p*p==; smaller multiples are already marked",
                "Time **O(n log log n)**, memory **O(n)**; fine up to ~==1e7=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "vector<bool> comp(n+1);",
                "for (int i = 2; i*i <= n; i++)",
                "  if (!comp[i])",
                "    for (int j = i*i; j <= n; j += i)",
                "      comp[j] = true;"
              ],
              "note": "prime = index >= 2 with comp false"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. SPF Sieve and Mistakes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`spf[x]` = smallest prime factor of x",
                "Repeat `x /= spf[x]` to factor any `x <= n` in ==O(log x)==",
                "Build once, answer many factorizations"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistakes",
              "text": "Inner loop from `2*i` wastes time: start at `i*i`. And `i*i` overflows int near 2^31: use ==long long==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fast Exponentiation (Binary Power)",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Fast Exponentiation (Binary Power)",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Idea",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Even n}: `a^n = (a^(n/2))^2`",
                "{blue:Odd n}: `a^n = a * a^(n-1)`",
                "==O(log n)== multiplies instead of O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Iterative Loop",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "long long res = 1; a %= m;",
                "while (n) {",
                "  if (n & 1) res = res * a % m;",
                "  a = a * a % m;",
                "  n >>= 1;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "reduce a first; res and a are long long"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Matrix power works the same: ==Fibonacci in O(log n)==",
                "Modulus near 1e18: `a*a` overflows, use ==__int128== or mulmod"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: 3^13",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Bit",
                "Set?",
                "a at step",
                "Multiply in"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "0",
                  "1",
                  "3^1",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "1",
                  "0",
                  "3^2",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "1",
                  "3^4",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "1",
                  "3^8",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "13 = 1101",
              "text": "3^13 = 3^1 * 3^4 * 3^8. Skipping `a %= m` or using `int` overflows."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why O(log n)?** n halves every loop",
                "**Which powers for 3^13?** 3^1, 3^4, 3^8",
                "**Modulus near 1e18?** `__int128` or mulmod"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
