    {
      "title": "Modular Inverse and nCr",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Modular Inverse and nCr",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Modular Inverse",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inverse of a: ==x== with `a*x ≡ 1 (mod m)`",
                "Exists only if ==gcd(a,m) = 1=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Modulus",
                "Method",
                "Cost"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Prime",
                  "Fermat: `a^(m-2) mod m`",
                  "O(log m)"
                ],
                [
                  "Composite",
                  "Extended Euclid (Fermat fails)",
                  "O(log m)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. nCr in O(1)",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "fact[0..N]",
                    "sub": "O(N)",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "invFact[N]",
                    "sub": "one pow",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Walk down",
                    "sub": "invFact[i-1]",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Query",
                    "sub": "O(1)",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "invFact[N] = power(fact[N], m-2);",
                "for (i = N; i > 0; i--)",
                "  invFact[i-1] = invFact[i] * i % m;",
                "// nCr = fact[n] * invFact[r] % m * invFact[n-r] % m"
              ],
              "note": "nCr = n! / (r!(n-r)!)"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pascal and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`C(n,r) = C(n-1,r-1) + C(n-1,r)`, O(n*r)",
                "Works for ==any modulus=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "n! mod m is {red:0} once n >= m",
                "r > n must return 0"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why not Fermat for composite m?** It needs prime m; use extended Euclid.",
                "**Why only one pow?** invFact[i-1] = invFact[i]*i % m."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
